# SSH Configuration for macOS Keychain Integration
#
# Purpose:
# This configuration enables seamless SSH authentication for git operations
# (push/pull) without repeatedly entering the SSH key passphrase.
#
# How it works:
# - AddKeysToAgent: Automatically adds SSH keys to the ssh-agent when used
# - UseKeychain: Stores the passphrase securely in macOS Keychain
# - IdentityFile: Specifies which SSH key to use for authentication
#
# Setup Instructions:
# 1. After installing dotfiles, run the following command ONCE to store your passphrase:
#    ssh-add --apple-use-keychain ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
#
# 2. Enter your passphrase when prompted. It will be stored in macOS Keychain.
#
# 3. Future git operations (push/pull) will use the stored passphrase automatically.
#
# Note: This configuration applies to all SSH hosts (Host *).
# You can add specific host configurations below if needed.

Host *
  AddKeysToAgent yes
  UseKeychain yes
  IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
